From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:37:55 -0400
Subject: feat: separators in the sidebar, from a row's menu

A row of the Space's list -- a Space pin or a tab -- can have a thin line
above it, as faint as the Clear line, in a band that stands the row lower,
to group the rows without a folder. Right-click a row for Add Separator
Above, or Remove Separator on a row that has one; nothing else adds one.
The line is the row's: it moves with it, goes when it closes, is carried
when the row's page is replaced and comes back after a restart as a
per-tab session value, as a tab's name does (sidebar Y45, GitHub issue
19). Not yet: a label, separators in folders, in the export file and in
folder sync.

Why: the owner, 2026-10-26 (GitHub issue 19, "build it now").
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the code.
